WEBVTT

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:32.470
Welcome back, glad to see you today.

00:00:32.470 --> 00:00:34.170
And today, let's just have some fun.

00:00:34.170 --> 00:00:35.710
Let's just do a quick little painting here

00:00:35.710 --> 00:00:38.370
that'll make you happy in here.

00:00:38.370 --> 00:00:42.900
I'm gonna start out with a little tiny bit of phthalo blue.

00:00:42.900 --> 00:00:45.420
I'll just beat it right into this large brush

00:00:45.420 --> 00:00:48.170
and start right up in here.

00:00:48.170 --> 00:00:51.230
Just sort of vary this, just work it around.

00:00:51.230 --> 00:00:53.610
Wanna leave some light areas in the sky.

00:00:53.610 --> 00:00:57.930
Don't wanna kill all the light areas.

00:00:57.930 --> 00:00:59.060
Just work it around.

00:01:07.420 --> 00:01:11.340
And let's see, that'll give us enough to start with.

00:01:11.340 --> 00:01:12.940
And while I've got this on the brush,

00:01:12.940 --> 00:01:14.440
add a little bit more of the blue

00:01:14.440 --> 00:01:17.530
and a tiny, tiny little bit of phthalo green.

00:01:17.530 --> 00:01:20.410
Not much, not much, it's very strong.

00:01:20.410 --> 00:01:21.640
Just a little bit.

00:01:21.640 --> 00:01:28.330
And we'll just come from out here,

00:01:28.330 --> 00:01:30.000
just very quickly drop in some.

00:01:30.670 --> 00:01:37.460
but it'll eventually be water.

00:01:37.460 --> 00:01:39.220
Now we can wash this old brush,

00:01:39.220 --> 00:01:49.700
excess paint thinner, cover the studio.

00:01:49.700 --> 00:01:52.240
Okay, now with a clean, dry brush,

00:01:52.240 --> 00:01:55.460
we're just gonna gently blend this out.

00:01:55.460 --> 00:01:57.660
Just blend it out.

00:01:57.660 --> 00:01:59.670
Have fun, enjoy.

00:02:00.160 --> 00:02:01.960
Don't try to kill all these little white areas.

00:02:01.960 --> 00:02:04.500
They end up making things happen in the sky.

00:02:04.500 --> 00:02:06.100
You don't end up with a sky that looks like

00:02:06.100 --> 00:02:08.590
you pulled the window shade down at night.

00:02:08.590 --> 00:02:10.970
Some action in it.

00:02:10.970 --> 00:02:14.770
Little things that are happening.

00:02:14.770 --> 00:02:17.440
Okay, there we are.

00:02:17.440 --> 00:02:22.200
Super nice, quick little way to make a happy little sky.

00:02:22.200 --> 00:02:27.820
I'm gonna take some Prussian blue and alizarin crimson.

00:02:27.820 --> 00:02:30.000
Now the Prussian blue is a

00:02:30.190 --> 00:02:32.750
100 times stronger than the crimson,

00:02:32.750 --> 00:02:40.730
so use very little blue and quite a bit of crimson.

00:02:40.730 --> 00:02:43.720
And if you want to test it, take a little white

00:02:43.720 --> 00:02:45.620
and put somewhere else and pull a little bit of the color

00:02:45.620 --> 00:02:46.960
and put it into it.

00:02:46.960 --> 00:02:48.360
That's really about the only way you can tell

00:02:48.360 --> 00:02:50.220
exactly what you have.

00:02:50.220 --> 00:02:53.260
This just looks black, it's so dark.

00:02:53.260 --> 00:02:57.260
Okay, so that's about what I'm looking for.

00:02:57.260 --> 00:02:59.190
So now we'll use the fan brush.

00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:01.380
a little bit of the color in here.

00:03:01.380 --> 00:03:03.380
Very little, very little.

00:03:03.380 --> 00:03:05.300
I want a very soft little painting today.

00:03:05.300 --> 00:03:07.550
And let's just go right up in here

00:03:07.550 --> 00:03:12.980
and just put us a little basic mountain shape,

00:03:12.980 --> 00:03:15.040
just however you want it.

00:03:15.040 --> 00:03:24.310
Just let it sort of go off into nothing over here.

00:03:24.310 --> 00:03:30.000
Gently pull some of that down, just a very basic

00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:33.330
shape, we're not looking for detail in this mountain.

00:03:33.330 --> 00:03:35.700
In our other series, we've really put a lot of detail

00:03:35.700 --> 00:03:37.700
into mountains, and this time,

00:03:37.700 --> 00:03:40.520
thought we'd do other things.

00:03:40.520 --> 00:03:43.050
We've done a lot of buildings in this series.

00:03:43.050 --> 00:03:45.660
Gonna do some more if what's over with.

00:03:45.660 --> 00:03:48.000
Okay, now with a large brush,

00:03:48.000 --> 00:03:56.470
just gonna grab a hole and pull it down, just like so.

00:03:56.470 --> 00:03:59.120
Don't spend a lot of time worrying about it,

00:03:59.120 --> 00:04:00.000
this is just a little

00:04:00.670 --> 00:04:04.930
A little mountain that's way back in the distance.

00:04:04.930 --> 00:04:16.050
Easy, that is.

00:04:16.050 --> 00:04:18.310
Now maybe, maybe there's one a little closer.

00:04:18.310 --> 00:04:21.860
Maybe just like a little foothill or something.

00:04:21.860 --> 00:04:24.410
Maybe it's just this.

00:04:24.410 --> 00:04:27.370
And we want it to be a little darker.

00:04:27.370 --> 00:04:30.000
A little bit darker.

00:04:30.120 --> 00:04:32.780
add a little more paint into this one.

00:04:32.780 --> 00:04:34.180
As these things get closer to you,

00:04:34.180 --> 00:04:35.660
allow 'em to get darker.

00:04:35.660 --> 00:04:40.950
That helps create distance in your painting.

00:04:40.950 --> 00:04:51.050
Very gently, we'll just pull this one.

00:04:51.050 --> 00:04:54.020
You can move this paint all over the canvas.

00:04:54.020 --> 00:04:59.000
The Magic White's underneath allows the paint to slide.

00:05:04.000 --> 00:05:07.330
And that quick, we have two very nice ranges of hills

00:05:07.330 --> 00:05:10.750
in the background here.

00:05:10.750 --> 00:05:13.840
Now, the only thing that separates these two

00:05:13.840 --> 00:05:17.610
is the light area in between and the difference in value.

00:05:17.610 --> 00:05:20.330
This one's much darker than the one that's far away,

00:05:20.330 --> 00:05:23.260
so it creates the illusion of distance already.

00:05:23.260 --> 00:05:28.310
Okay, let's take a little bit of sap green

00:05:28.310 --> 00:05:30.000
and throw it right into this purple color.

00:05:30.280 --> 00:05:35.330
we have, so we have sap green, a little bit of blue,

00:05:35.330 --> 00:05:39.030
and alizarin crimson.

00:05:39.030 --> 00:05:40.390
Just put it all together.

00:05:40.390 --> 00:05:46.800
This should be predominantly green.

00:05:46.800 --> 00:05:51.690
Okay, let's just take the one-inch brush

00:05:51.690 --> 00:05:53.140
and load it full of paint.

00:05:53.140 --> 00:05:54.220
Let's pull it through the paint,

00:05:54.220 --> 00:05:57.720
put a lot of paint into the bristles, a lot of paint.

00:06:00.670 --> 00:06:02.170
Maybe we'll lighten that a tiny bit.

00:06:02.170 --> 00:06:04.630
I want to add the least little amount of white to it,

00:06:04.630 --> 00:06:07.280
just to lighten it up a little.

00:06:07.280 --> 00:06:08.320
A little bit of white.

00:06:08.320 --> 00:06:11.780
Don't get carried away.

00:06:11.780 --> 00:06:13.870
Got a lot of paint in the bristles.

00:06:13.870 --> 00:06:15.970
Now, let's go right up in here,

00:06:15.970 --> 00:06:21.620
put some little distant trees back.

00:06:21.620 --> 00:06:25.350
Let the brush work, let the brush work.

00:06:31.820 --> 00:06:33.460
as far away little trees.

00:06:33.460 --> 00:06:44.200
As many trees in your world as you want.

00:06:44.200 --> 00:06:48.880
So happen, let 'em happen, tell me about 'em.

00:06:48.880 --> 00:06:50.800
Enjoy, have fun.

00:07:00.000 --> 00:07:02.800
See how easy it is to make little distant trees?

00:07:02.800 --> 00:07:04.340
It really gives the illusion of trees

00:07:04.340 --> 00:07:10.230
that are far, far away.

00:07:10.230 --> 00:07:13.270
Over here I want them just to sort of fade out.

00:07:13.270 --> 00:07:14.830
I want this whole side of this painting

00:07:14.830 --> 00:07:17.320
