Put some little things down in here.

00:20:06.810 --> 00:20:09.170
Now let's get down here and play with the water a little bit.

00:20:09.170 --> 00:20:11.480
We'll take a little bit of Magic White,

00:20:11.480 --> 00:20:13.160
a little bit of the Firm White,

00:20:13.160 --> 00:20:15.970
and put the Magic White in just to thin it a little.

00:20:15.970 --> 00:20:20.170
And we can begin coming right in here,

00:20:20.170 --> 00:20:23.330
bring some water right up to the land.

00:20:32.880 --> 00:20:35.720
With the old fan brush, it's very simple.

00:20:35.720 --> 00:20:39.860
You can do it in just a matter of seconds.

00:20:39.860 --> 00:20:45.960
The brush is a super, super brush.

00:20:45.960 --> 00:20:47.810
You have to make friends with it, though.

00:20:47.810 --> 00:20:50.170
It takes a little while.

00:20:50.170 --> 00:20:53.520
It's not the easiest brush in the world to master.

00:20:53.520 --> 00:20:57.030
But once you do, oh my gosh, what you can do with it.

00:20:57.030 --> 00:20:58.300
Once you can do with it,

00:20:58.300 --> 00:21:00.000
entire paintings can be done very

00:21:00.000 --> 00:21:12.340
easily with just a fan brush.

00:21:12.340 --> 00:21:18.020
Just put some little indications here and there.

00:21:18.020 --> 00:21:22.540
Okay, now, now we can get crazy.

00:21:22.540 --> 00:21:24.970
Let's take some brown, Van Dyke brown,

00:21:24.970 --> 00:21:26.350
a little bit of burnt umber in it.

00:21:26.350 --> 00:21:28.190
Not much, just a little umber.

00:21:28.190 --> 00:21:29.670
Just a little bit of umber.

00:21:31.150 --> 00:21:37.640
Maybe it will come with some color.

00:21:37.640 --> 00:21:38.880
Don't be afraid of it.

00:21:38.880 --> 00:21:50.750
Just throw it in a little bit more.

00:21:50.750 --> 00:21:54.820
Feed the dark in order for the light to show.

00:21:54.820 --> 00:21:58.700
All we're doing here, just adding some dark.

00:21:58.700 --> 00:22:00.000
Let's just let this come all the way across.

00:22:00.060 --> 00:22:02.470
What the heck, what the heck.

00:22:02.470 --> 00:22:06.770
This is our world, so we can do what we want to.

00:22:06.770 --> 00:22:12.520
Okay, maybe, maybe, maybe,

00:22:12.520 --> 00:22:16.250
maybe you have a happy little tree that lives right here.

00:22:16.250 --> 00:22:23.000
So we put some dark in, same colors of dark, just,

00:22:23.000 --> 00:22:30.000
there's one, I see one right there, right there.

00:22:35.120 --> 00:22:37.210
All we're doing is just laying in some dark.

00:22:37.210 --> 00:22:42.760
Not really worried about shape or form yet.

00:22:42.760 --> 00:22:47.040
Take a little bit of the highlight color,

00:22:47.040 --> 00:22:50.950
very lightly, just touch, pull.

00:22:50.950 --> 00:22:54.370
This is brown and white, burnt umber.

00:22:54.370 --> 00:22:58.320
You gently just pull, like so.

00:23:00.350 --> 00:23:06.970
Now we can come back and begin laying in all kinds of little,

00:23:06.970 --> 00:23:09.900
little things happening all over here.

00:23:09.900 --> 00:23:11.060
Need something a little lighter,

00:23:11.060 --> 00:23:13.140
it's not gonna show right there, so we'll just,

00:23:13.140 --> 00:23:17.670
there, that's what I was looking for.

00:23:17.670 --> 00:23:20.670
Knew it was in there, we just had to find it.

00:23:20.670 --> 00:23:23.170
There's just all kinds of little things

00:23:23.170 --> 00:23:24.580
growing right along in here.

00:23:31.600 --> 00:23:33.950
Just drop 'em in.

00:23:33.950 --> 00:23:38.040
Highlight on 'em.

00:23:38.040 --> 00:23:40.760
Just nice, soft, little fern-looking things.

00:23:40.760 --> 00:23:58.680
Next week, tell you what let's do next week.

00:23:58.680 --> 00:24:00.000
Let's do the little.

00:24:00.090 --> 00:24:01.650
the little painting that we animated

00:24:01.650 --> 00:24:04.360
at the beginning of the show, the little lighthouse.

00:24:04.360 --> 00:24:07.000
So, have a black canvas ready.

00:24:07.000 --> 00:24:12.600
We'll do a black one next week.

00:24:12.600 --> 00:24:15.970
A few little highlights right up in here.

00:24:15.970 --> 00:24:21.220
Just drop 'em on, let 'em go.

00:24:21.220 --> 00:24:25.700
And sort of layer these,

00:24:25.700 --> 00:24:27.490
it'll give distance to your painting.

00:24:36.940 --> 00:24:39.290
All kinds of little things happening.

00:24:39.290 --> 00:24:40.750
Wherever you think they should be,

00:24:40.750 --> 00:24:56.390
that's where they should be.

00:24:56.390 --> 00:24:57.560
Just here and there.

00:24:57.560 --> 00:25:00.000
Gently scrape in a few little sticks and twigs.

00:25:02.300 --> 00:25:09.730
all over, wherever you think there should be

00:25:09.730 --> 00:25:11.870
a little twig showing here and there.

00:25:11.870 --> 00:25:13.350
Just drop it in.

00:25:13.350 --> 00:25:15.750
And all I'm doing is using the point of the knife,

00:25:15.750 --> 00:25:17.420
cutting right through the paint,

00:25:17.420 --> 00:25:20.040
and allowing a little bit of the canvas to show through.

00:25:20.040 --> 00:25:24.830
We're not really putting any color on the canvas.

00:25:24.830 --> 00:25:29.540
Just like that.

00:25:38.190 --> 00:25:45.160
Couple over in this area that you can see in the background.

00:25:45.160 --> 00:25:51.650
Let's take right in here.

00:25:51.650 --> 00:25:54.060
Maybe just add a little tiny bit more

00:25:54.060 --> 00:25:58.680
that's growing right down, almost at ground level, like so.

00:26:05.180 --> 00:26:07.390
Okay, I think we have a painting

00:26:07.390 --> 00:26:09.910
that's about ready for a signature.

00:26:09.910 --> 00:26:12.090
So let's take the liner brush,

00:26:12.090 --> 00:26:14.080
a little bit of the thin oil,

00:26:14.080 --> 00:26:16.020
and I'll go right into some permanent red.

00:26:16.020 --> 00:26:19.720
That's sort of my color for signatures.

00:26:19.720 --> 00:26:22.710
And we'll just drop a little signature,

00:26:22.710 --> 00:26:26.690
right there, like so.

00:26:26.690 --> 00:26:29.410
As I say, next week, have your black canvas ready,

00:26:30.570 --> 00:26:33.200
and we'll do that little lighthouse.

00:26:33.200 --> 00:26:37.430
That's such a fun painting, I think you'll really enjoy it.

00:26:37.430 --> 00:26:40.810
There we go, signed, sealed, and delivered.

00:26:40.810 --> 00:26:42.930
And the old clock on the wall tells me

00:26:42.930 --> 00:26:45.370
I got to get out of here and leave you for this week.

00:26:45.370 --> 00:26:47.360
We're looking forward to seeing you again.

00:26:47.360 --> 00:26:49.350
Happy painting, bye-bye.
